{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.FBorBorromeanObservable","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.FBorBorromeanObservable","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ocneanu_factor_twelve_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ocneanu_factor_twelve_categorical","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/f-bor-borromean-observable.lean#L103-L118","doc":"**The categorical integer 12 of the F_Bor substrate identity.**\n\n`12 = mult · bind = 2 · 6 = dim V_{(2,1)} · |S_3|` — a categorical count\n(trace-dominant irrep dimension times the symmetric-group order).\n\nHISTORICAL / REFUTED PROVENANCE: an earlier reading identified 12 as the\ninverse of an Ocneanu leading-pole coefficient −1/12, claiming\n`tr_M(β_Bor, q) ~ −1/(12 · q^10)` as q → 0. This is **refuted for β_Bor**:\nits Markov trace has a q^(-4) pole of coefficient 1, not q^(-10)·(−1/12)\n(the −1/12·q^(-10) pole belongs to the measured no-interface braid, a\ndifferent word). Retracted 2026-05-25; re-confirmed in the 2026-08-22 F_Bor\nred-team (docs/audits/2026-08-22-mp-fbor-massformula-redteam.md). The −1/12\nprovenance is NOT part of the derivation; only the categorical count `2 · 6`\nis. (Name retained for reference stability; the \"ocneanu\" in it is historical.)\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bar_pair_factor_two_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bar_pair_factor_two_categorical","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/f-bor-borromean-observable.lean#L84-L101","doc":"**Bar-pair partition count (categorical).**\n\nThe integer 2 in the F_Bor-based substrate identity counts the\nbar-pair partitions in the proton's H_3(q) Wedderburn\ndecomposition: (3) and (1,1,1) form a transpose pair under bar\ninvolution.\n\nProved upstream in `YLambdaQSchur.lean\nyLambdaQSchur_transpose_pair`:\n  y_(3)(q) · y_{(3)^T}(q) = 1/[3]_q!²\n\nwhere (3)^T = (1,1,1).  The bar-pair has exactly 2 elements;\nself-conjugate (2,1) is the third partition of 3 not in this\npair.\n\nThe bridge from this combinatorial fact to the \"factor 2 in\nthe mass formula\" is the open structural step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.F_Bor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.F_Bor","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/f-bor-borromean-observable.lean#L69-L82","doc":"The natural categorical observable\n`F_Bor(q) := |tr_M(β_Bor, q)| · [3]_q! / q^3`.\n\nCombines the Lean-proved Borromean Markov trace with the\nq-factorial normalisation, shifted by content q^3 (the content\nsum of the partition (3) ⊢ 3).\n\nInherits the linearly ordered field structure from\n`trM_borromean_abs`'s `|·|`; `qFact_three` (only `[Field R]`)\ncomposes on the shared `Field R`. The archimedean evaluation\n`F_Bor (q_0 : ℝ)` resolves with `R := ℝ` downstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qFact_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qFact_three","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/f-bor-borromean-observable.lean#L60-L67","doc":"The q-factorial `[3]_q! = (q² + 1 + q⁻²)(q + q⁻¹)`.\n\nMirror of the proved `qFactorial_three` from `YLambdaQSchur.lean`\n(restated here for self-contained use). Purely categorical\n(field inverse + integer powers, no order), so the base ring is\nthe weakest that admits the construction, `[Field R]` (§7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_abs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.trM_borromean_abs","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/f-bor-borromean-observable.lean#L44-L58","doc":"The Borromean Markov-trace closed form\n`|tr_M(β_Bor, q)| = (4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶) / (h² + 4)`.\n\nMirror of the proved `trM_borromean` in\n`BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean` (restated here for self-contained\nuse in the F_Bor observable).\n\nThe `|·|` is the only post-archimedean construct (it requires an\norder), so the base ring is the generic linearly ordered field\n`[Field R] [LinearOrder R] [IsStrictOrderedRing R]` rather than\n`ℝ` — the archimedean evaluation at `q_0 : ℝ` happens downstream\n(§7c). ","signatureChunk":0}]}